WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:04.779
Getting in shape for a superhero movie is
practically half the battle, so it's exhilarating

00:00:04.779 --> 00:00:08.780
to watch an actor rise to the occasion of
getting ripped for his or her role.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:13.580
From Scarlett Johansson's acrobatics as Black
Widow to Chris Hemsworth's otherworldly biceps,

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.340
the cast has to almost become otherworldly
themselves before they can appear on-screen

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.070
for the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:24.010
And with Avengers: Infinity War arriving as
easily the biggest, most bombastic Marvel

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:28.310
film yet, there's no doubt the massive cast
had to really crank it into overdrive to get

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.610
fit for the big battle.

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:35.060
Here's how our heroes shaped up to show down
with Thanos in Infinity War.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.680
Heavy lifting

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:41.710
Sebastian Stan's friendship with his personal
trainer Don Saladino is pretty well documented.

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:45.540
They're all over each other's Instagram feeds,
and Saladino was a key player in getting Stan

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.460
shredded for his role as the Winter Soldier.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.900
Stan stuck with Saladino while prepping for
the third Avengers outing and revealed that

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:54.970
the key to their training method is to keep
it heavy.

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:58.850
Most bodybuilding workouts tend to involve
lifting lighter weights at higher rates of

00:00:58.850 --> 00:00:59.850
repetition.

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:03.730
Instead, Stan and Saladino kicked every day
off with big, bulky lifts.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:08.000
There are videos online of their workouts,
with plenty of bodybuilding-style lifts.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.369
"You know you get up on the morning.

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:10.979
You know, it's not…

00:01:10.979 --> 00:01:13.710
Even on the weekend if it is, getting there
for an hour.

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.909
You know, get through it.

00:01:14.909 --> 00:01:16.020
Push yourself through it.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.020
Your tired.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:18.020
Do something."

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:21.820
It clearly got the job done, as Stan is looking
killer as the Winter Soldier.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:25.009
"Not bad for the end of the world."

00:01:25.009 --> 00:01:26.719
Eating right

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:30.679
Exercise is obviously very important to getting
an actor in shape to play a superhero, but

00:01:30.679 --> 00:01:32.600
dieting can be just as crucial.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:37.380
For her return as the Scarlet Witch, Elizabeth
Olsen kept nutrition in mind.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:42.200
Olsen's nutritionist Philip Goglia has openly
discussed Olsen's goals for Scarlet Witch

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:45.619
in the new film and says she focused heavily
on body composition.

00:01:45.619 --> 00:01:50.430
This meant her diet was radically restructured,
and she eliminated gluten, dairy, and yeast

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:55.039
altogether, and ate seven to eight meals per
day, largely consisting of fruits, vegetables,

00:01:55.039 --> 00:01:57.130
and chicken and fish as proteins.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:01.130
It honestly sounds like a nice diet, right
up until you remember it means saying no to

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:02.399
pizza.

00:02:02.399 --> 00:02:03.829
Mixing it up

00:02:03.829 --> 00:02:07.899
Chris Evans has been hitting the gym for nearly
ten years now to get in shape to play the

00:02:07.899 --> 00:02:12.361
Star-Spangled Avenger, Captain America, so
to keep his routine from getting stale, Evans

00:02:12.361 --> 00:02:15.450
has incorporated quite a bit of variety into
his routine.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:19.900
Evans' doesn't play up any singular exercise
over others and instead hops around from body-weight

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:24.440
movements like pull-ups to weighted ones like
classic bicep curls and kettle weights.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:28.250
The most surprising thing about all of his
workouts is just how approachable they are.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:32.080
Sure, they're going to be a little intense
for anyone who's never done them, but Evans'

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:35.960
workout can probably be done on your own at
your local gym.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:37.530
The buddy system

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:41.200
Scarlett Johansson has been playing Black
Widow for nearly ten years now, and those

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.970
constant workouts can get to be awfully monotonous.

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:48.970
So Johansson's solution is to go to the gym
with a friend, in this case, co-star Sebastian

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:49.970
Stan.

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:53.810
While it doesn't seem to have been an everyday
thing, Johansson tagged along for some workouts

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:56.600
with Stan and his trainer in preparations
for the shoot.

00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:00.970
Who doesn't love the mental image of Black
Widow yelling at a sweaty, exhausted Bucky

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:03.580
to squeeze out one more rep?

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:05.120
Making arm day

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:09.580
To become the God of Thunder, Chris Hemsworth
has to get pretty huge all over, but there's

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.560
one area he seems to pay special attention
to.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.980
"He's so… he's huge!"

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:19.620
Thor's hammer-swinging arms need to be huge,
and since his get-up tends to be sleeveless,

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.230
his trainer maxes out the days they work those
muscles.

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:27.730
Hemsworth is already a pretty big dude, but
he's by no means Thor-sized at all times.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:31.080
It makes the work he puts into getting big
enough to play the god of thunder all the

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:32.080
more impressive.

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:34.200
"Are you mocking me?"

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.200
Fight training

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:40.550
Even the most artistic superhero films feature
a few central scuffles, so it's not just about

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:41.740
looking tough.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:45.560
The actors also have to convince audiences
that their sparring techniques are legitimate

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:46.830
during action scenes.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:50.740
And since his character is arguably one of
the most hand-to-hand fighters of the bunch,

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:54.390
Tom Holland doubled down and got into the
ring at a boxing gym.

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:58.510
Holland has been boxing for some time now,
but incorporating boxing into his workouts

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:02.550
prepping for Infinity War ensured that the
muscle he put on for his newest outing as

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:04.700
Spider-Man wouldn't just be cosmetic.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:09.380
Holland can throw a punch for real, which
lends a cool air of legitimacy to any moments

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:11.510
in which Spidey's fists get to work.

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:13.290
Odd inspiration

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:18.819
Dave Bautista has now gotten in Drax the Destroyer
shape for two Marvel films, and he managed

00:04:18.819 --> 00:04:24.249
to avoid plateauing for Infinity War by taking
inspiration from a costar's progress.

00:04:24.249 --> 00:04:27.210
"A handsome, muscular man."

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:31.460
Josh Brolin didn't have to get ripped to play
Thanos, thanks to the magic of visual effects,

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:34.599
but Thanos isn't the only comic character
he's playing this year.

00:04:34.599 --> 00:04:39.979
He'll also be appearing in Deadpool 2 as Cable,
and he definitely got jacked for that role.

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:44.620
Brolin is on the older side for a superhero
actor, and Bautista took a good bit of inspiration

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:47.610
from seeing his costar get buff for his turn
as Cable.

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:51.319
He publicly talked about how it inspired him
to train even harder to prep for his role

00:04:51.319 --> 00:04:57.240
as Drax, getting the character pumped up to
maximum levels of destructive capabilities.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:58.330
Keeping secrets

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:02.130
Although many of his co-stars are happy to
open the books on their fitness regimens for

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:06.789
the MCU, Chadwick Boseman likes to keep a
few of his cards close to the chest.

00:05:06.789 --> 00:05:11.680
Black Panther and Infinity War were shot around
the same time, so Boseman's fitness routine

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:14.389
doubled as preparation for both appearances.

00:05:14.389 --> 00:05:17.979
While he later opened up a bit more, Boseman
actually kept pretty mum when asked how he

00:05:17.979 --> 00:05:19.789
was getting in shape for the film, saying:

00:05:19.789 --> 00:05:23.010
"A lot of strength and flexibility, but I'm
not going to say any more.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.969
[...] How do you know it's not kickin' right
now?

00:05:24.969 --> 00:05:26.849
I might be covering something up."

00:05:26.849 --> 00:05:31.479
In other words, Boseman was suggesting that
he was already in superhero shape long before

00:05:31.479 --> 00:05:35.900
he signed up to play T'Challa . That's about
as much modesty as you might expect from the

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.330
King of Wakanda.

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:39.939
"I never freeze."

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:41.370
Learning the blade

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:45.060
Sometimes weightlifting and cardio alone won't
cut it when it comes to preparing for the

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.710
physicality of a role.

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:51.949
For Black Panther star Danai Gurira, weapons
training was just as key as anything to ready

00:05:51.949 --> 00:05:52.960
her for the role.

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:57.479
Gurira's history of sword combat training
for her part as the katana-wielding Michonne

00:05:57.479 --> 00:06:00.910
on TV's The Walking Dead came in handy for
the actress.

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:05.969
Her MCU character Okoye the leader of the
Dora Milaje, might not use a katana herself,

00:06:05.969 --> 00:06:09.600
but Gurira found the combat training for Michonne
helped tremendously.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:13.759
Her ability to swing a spear was completely
convincing in Black Panther, and considering

00:06:13.759 --> 00:06:17.750
she and her army will have their hands full
in Avengers: Infinity War, we're in for a

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:21.120
pretty awesome fight when the new film drops.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:22.820
"Boom!"

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:23.980
Thanks for watching!

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:26.370
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:28.880
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

